[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1386","stub":{"id":"1386","section":"2) Piercefield to Parmenter Site","altname":"","river":"Raquette","difficulty":"IItoV","states":["USA-NYO"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"migration-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"1950","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"An alternate putin is the town beach on river left.\n\n_Note: coordinates and distances are verified by GPS._","id":"100006","location":{"latitude":"44.234100341796875","longitude":"-74.57109832763672"},"name":"Public Beach","distance":"0.4054","photoID":"0","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"portage","description":"This is a serious drop which you'll want to scout (and maybe portage). According to Squires, the line changes with the water level. At 1700 cfs, there's a sneak along far river right.","id":"10176","location":{"latitude":"44.3114128112793","longitude":"-74.71499633789062"},"name":"Moody Falls","distance":"13.8033","photoID":"50784","difficulty":"IV+","approximate":true},{"type":"portage","description":"That hole is _munchy_. It looks like it might weaken in the middle, but with a loaded boat and no one to save my sorry butt, I walked it at 1700 cfs","id":"100005","location":{"latitude":"44.323204040527344","longitude":"-74.71527099609375"},"name":"Upper Jamestown Falls","distance":"14.7582","photoID":"50786","difficulty":"IV+","approximate":false},{"type":"portage","description":"Squires lists Upper Jamestown as a IV+/5.0, and Lower Jamestown as bigger and badder--likely a portage. At 1700 cfs, I found that I wanted to walk Upper J, but I found a far-right sneak at Lower J.\n\nIf you don't want to paddle to the Parmenter Site, you can take out 250 yards below, at a hard-to-find (from the road) dirt road.","id":"10177","location":{"latitude":"44.32470703125","longitude":"-74.71542358398438"},"name":"Lower Jamestown Falls","distance":"15.0069","photoID":"50778","difficulty":"V","approximate":true},{"type":"takeout","description":"According to Squires, there's a takeout just downstream of Jamestown, tough to see from Rte. 56. I'm skeptical; I think the dirt road might be private property, but I'm listing this spot in case you can find a way to get to it and save yourself two miles of paddling.","id":"100007","location":{"latitude":"44.32741928100586","longitude":"-74.71832275390625"},"name":"Alternate takeout","distance":"15.2458","photoID":"0","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"8yVKoPTV9lGK66Rd9cCZ8","title":"ADK White","post_date":"2024-06-27 20:37:39+00","detail":null,"user":{"name":"Olivia Primeaux"}}],"photos":[{"id":"50779","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"194555","description":"1700 cfs","caption":"Bad Day for Someone","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Ratt Boy (KHCC, FLOW)","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/50779","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/50779"}},{"id":"50780","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"194555","description":"1700 cfs","caption":"Piercefield Dam","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Ratt Boy (KHCC, FLOW)","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/50780","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/50780"}},{"id":"50781","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"194555","description":"1700 cfs","caption":"Burnt Island","poi_name":"Burnt Island","subject":"","author":"Ratt Boy (KHCC, FLOW)","poi_id":"10173","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/50781","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/50781"}},{"id":"50782","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"194555","description":"1700 cfs","caption":"Moosehead","poi_name":"Moosehead","subject":"","author":"Ratt Boy (KHCC, FLOW)","poi_id":"10175","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/50782","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/50782"}},{"id":"50786","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"194555","description":"1700 cfs","caption":"The Hole at Upper Jamestown","poi_name":"Upper Jamestown","subject":"","author":"Ratt Boy (KHCC, FLOW)","poi_id":"100005","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/50786","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/50786"}},{"id":"50778","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"194555","description":"1700 cfs","caption":"Lower Jamestown","poi_name":"Lower Jamestown","subject":"","author":"Ratt Boy (KHCC, FLOW)","poi_id":"10177","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/50778","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/50778"}},{"id":"50783","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"194555","description":"1700 cfs","caption":"Moosehead","poi_name":"Moosehead","subject":"","author":"Ratt Boy (KHCC, FLOW)","poi_id":"10175","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/50783","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/50783"}},{"id":"50784","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"194555","description":"1700 cfs","caption":"Top Part of Moody Falls","poi_name":"Moody Falls","subject":"","author":"Ratt Boy (KHCC, FLOW)","poi_id":"10176","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/50784","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/50784"}}],"detail":{"id":"1386","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"Assuming Class III is familiar to you, the first challenge is the Upper Sols and Lower Sols (around Sols Island). Go left around the island. Upper Sols increases in difficulty and the final part is class IV and can be scouted and carried on the Left. Then, flatwater and class II rapids alternate. The 5.7-mile Moosehead Stillwater follows, giving a relaxed time to enjoy turtles basking in the sun and other wildlife and flowers. Then Moosehead Rapids (class II-III) are 1.25 miles long with no portage trail. Next up, on a right turn, stay to the right of an island so you are ready to scout or portage Moody Falls, a class IV/V. The lower part is easier than the upper part. After Moody Falls, some carry out (or in and upstream to run Moody Falls) to NY 56. After less than a mile of flatwater, one encounters Jamestown Falls. Both Upper and Lower Jamestown Falls are impressive class V's. The national slalom team used the Falls as a training site in 1988 with flows controlled by the powerhouse.\n\nThe Parmenter site is a takeout. You can drive to the water when the campground is open or walk out to NY 56 on an asphalt road in the off season. Be aware that when there is a release at Piercefield, the beginning of the release will take several hours to travel the 14 miles to Moody Falls.\n\nThere is one release scheduled each year, as well as natural flow opportunities. The scheduled release is on the last Saturday of June and lasts 5 hours. Information on releases can be found at 800-452-1742, and using the code: 365130.\n\nSubmitted by Betty Lou Bailey of the Adirondack Mountain Club\n\nDennis Squires' book lists this as a good (and beautiful) overnighter, which typically runs until early June.\n\n**Potsdam - Malone Area Reaches**\n\n[Chateaugay](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1284/) [Deer (Dickinson Center)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1289/)\n\n[Deer (Dickinson Center to Lawrenceville)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1290/) [Grass (1. Lampsons Falls to Downerville)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1310/)\n\n[Grass (Sec. 3)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1312/) [Grass (Sec. 4)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1311/)\n\n[Jordan](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1329/)[Little Trout](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1339/)\n\n[Marble](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1342/) [Meacham Lake Outlet](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4250/)\n\n[Raquette Sec. 3) Hannawa Falls](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/3747/)[Raquette 2) Piercefield to Parmenter Site](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1386/)\n\n[Raquette Sec. 4) Stone Valley](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1387/) [Salmon](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1406/)\n\n[Salmon (Chasm Falls)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4099/) [St. Regis](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1427/)\n\n[St. Regis, E. Branch](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1428/) [St. Regis, Middle Branch (Sec. 1)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1429/)\n\n[St. Regis, Middle Branch (Sec. 2)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1430/) [St. Regis, Middle Branch (Sec. 3)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1431/)\n\n[St. Regis, Middle Branch (Sec. 4.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1432/) [St. Regis, W. Branch (Sec. 1)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1435/)\n\n[St. Regis, W. Branch (Sec. 2)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1433/) [St. Regis, W. Branch (Sec. 3)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1434/)\n\n[Trout Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1446/)\n\n**[Google Map of New York Whitewater](https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=zjdnDE8H0TLg.kJnMWGapL4xk)**\n\n**[New York Whitewater Paddlers Facebook Group](http